# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #method-parts; Codex OPUS-CODEX-20261015-24 Q1 (a)): the cursor i of the for head of S is a
# place S requires of its data. D has total but no i, so the call admission fails when the program runs, before the
# loop: the implicit call throw, taken by catch: call. D\total keeps 5. Entry 7.
S:
    int: total 0
    for: int(i, 0) (i < 3) i++
        total: total + i
    end: for
end: S
D:
    int: total 5
end: D
fn: run () int
    int: r 82
    call: S D
    catch: call ()
        r: 83
        if: D\total = 5
            r: 7
    ---
return: r
int: got run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
